Léa, a toddler girl with a stocky build, chin-length straight brown hair, loose bangs at her eyebrows, and brown eyes, wearing a red knit cardigan, grey trousers, and brown ankle boots, clutches the cuff of Henri's overcoat with both hands, tugging firmly as she looks up toward him with wide eyes, raised brows, and parted lips. Beside her, Henri, an elderly man with a slim build, stooped posture, short wavy combed gray hair, brown eyes, and a full gray beard, dressed in a long grey wool overcoat, an orange wool scarf, a blue checked shirt, brown corduroy trousers, and black lace-up shoes, stands facing down at her with a gentle, level brow and attentive eyes. Directly at Léa's feet on the wet dark grey timber planks of the covered wooden footbridge, the dark shape CHR001—a solid, flat, near-black silhouette of a slim, upright human figure with a smooth featureless head and long thin limbs, showing no eyes, mouth, or clothing—lies elongated and flat across the walkway. Overhead, the heavy dark timber trusses and diagonal wooden braces of the bridge roof frame the corridor, while narrow slatted wall openings reveal the muted orange and brown autumn foliage of the riverbank outside in the dim dusk light. In the background walkway, two distant pedestrians walk away—an adult in a charcoal rain jacket and dark pants, and another in a beige coat and white trousers. Medium shot at floor level inside the wooden bridge.

---METADATA---
