A close-up at the curved white enamel rim of the bathtub frames Léa, a toddler girl with chin-length straight brown hair with bangs, brown eyes, and soft rounded cheeks, wearing a purple cotton pyjama top, leaning her head close to Élodie's ear. Léa's eyes are turned intently toward Élodie, her mouth shaped in an urgent whisper with raised, worried brows, while keeping her face turned firmly away from the flat dark shape CHR001—a featureless, solid black silhouette extending along the upper curve of the enamel rim behind them. Élodie, a young adult woman with wavy light brown hair falling past her shoulder, wearing a thick yellow turtleneck sweater and her silver necklace, tilts her head down toward Léa, her expression neutral and calm with soft brows and a gently listening mouth beneath the gleaming chrome tap mounted against the white wall tiles.

